tes in America are women so we're  trying to chip away at an economic model  so in the last collective bargaining we  tripled the top player pay in which  Britney is one of the greatest players  ever to play the game so she was making  the super max as well as you can make  now up to seven hundred thousand dollars  for your four and a half month season  here but we we are we're literally  transforming and players are also  choosing to stay home we have 10 players  under player marketing agreements where  we'll pay those players million and a  half dollars over the course of the off  season we also have players who are  doing broadcast like a Candace Parker  and a Chana gumacay and we also have  Skyler Diggins out in Phoenix and Kia  nurse up in Toronto doing broadcast in  our off season when it's the season for  the NBA as well as  um college basketball a lot of our our  players are now assistant coaches and  things so we're finding opportunities  internships other things to make sure  that the players can make some money in  the off season in addition to driving  higher pay during our season  yeah so more more work to be done there  Kathy but we can all focus on the good  news today Brittany Greiner steps back  on American soil just a few hours ago uh  Kathy thank you very much for sharing  some time with us this morning  thank you so much  well thank you
 

